<title>JAPAN: Japan to review corporate tax in 98/99 reforms - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan to review corporate tax in 98/99 reforms - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka told parliament's Upper House on Thursday that corporate taxes would be reviewed as part of an overall reform of Japan's tax system planned for fiscal 1998/99.</p>
<p>He said the review will be made in an effort to lower corporate taxes to levels seen in other countries.</p>
<p>Mitsuzuka reiterated that a review of Japan's securities transaction taxes and land taxes will also be considered in planned overall taxation reforms.</p>
</text>
